      "slug": "spike-stitch-g43",
      "term": "Spike stitch",
      "definition": "A dc stitch worked by inserting the hook one or more rows below the current row, then drawing up a long loop to the working row height before completing the stitch. Creates a diagonal spike of colour."
    },
    {
      "slug": "colour-carry-g43",
      "term": "Colour carry",
      "definition": "Keeping the unused yarn at the back of the work, carried along the row, so it is ready to pick up when needed. Avoids too many loose ends."
    }
